---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="FAQs — HUE Co." description="Frequently asked questions about permanent jewelry at HUE Co. Does it hurt? Can I remove it? Is it waterproof? All the answers.">

<!-- ── Hero ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<section class="section--dark article-hero">
  <div class="container container--narrow">
    <span class="eyebrow eyebrow--light">Common Questions</span>
    <h1 class="section-title section-title--xl article-hero__title">Frequently Asked Questions</h1>
    <p class="section-subtitle">Honest answers. No marketing language.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ── FAQs ───────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<section class="section section--cream">
  <div class="container container--narrow">

    <div class="faq-list">

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-summary">Does it hurt?</summary>
        <div class="faq-body">
          <p>No. The weld is a brief spark — less than a second — and it doesn't touch your skin. The only thing that contacts your body is the chain itself. Most clients feel nothing at all. A few notice a faint warmth in the chain immediately after the weld, which dissipates in seconds. We've had clients with significant medical anxiety and sensory sensitivities complete the process without any discomfort.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-summary">How long does it take?</summary>
        <div class="faq-body">
          <p>About 30 minutes for a single chain, start to finish. This includes consultation, chain selection, measuring, and the weld itself. The weld is under ten seconds. Stacking sessions (3+ chains) run approximately 60 minutes. Bridal and event bookings vary depending on group size — contact us for a custom estimate.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-summary">Can I remove it?</summary>
        <div class="faq-body">
          <p>Yes. Removal is always free. Book a removal appointment online and we'll cut it off in under 60 seconds using a small pair of flush cutters. There's no damage to your skin, and the chain itself remains largely intact. Some clients keep the chain and re-weld it later. Removal is not a judgment — it's part of the service.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-summary">Is it waterproof?</summary>
        <div class="faq-body">
          <p>Yes. All three metal tiers at HUE Co. are waterproof and safe for daily wear. Swimming, showering, exercising, sleeping — none of these require removing your piece. After ocean or chlorine exposure, a quick rinse with fresh water helps maintain the chain's finish. That's the only maintenance you need.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-summary">What if it breaks?</summary>
        <div class="faq-body">
          <p>It can happen if the chain gets caught on something and pulled with force — a towel hook, a zipper, an unexpected tug. Within 30 days of your appointment, we re-weld for free. This is your warranty. After 30 days, re-welds are $20 for Tier 1 and 2, and $35 for Tier 3. Bring both pieces of the chain. The 30-day warranty resets on the new weld.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-summary">Can I get an MRI?</summary>
        <div class="faq-body">
          <p>You should always inform your medical team of all jewelry, including permanent jewelry. Most micro-welded chains can be removed quickly before imaging if your team determines it's necessary — and removal is always free at HUE Co. Stainless steel and gold are generally non-ferromagnetic (they are not attracted to magnets), but MRI protocols vary, and your radiologist's guidance takes priority. Book a removal appointment and we'll have you out of the chair in seconds.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-summary">Is there an age requirement?</summary>
        <div class="faq-body">
          <p>Guests under 18 are welcome at HUE Co., but require a parent or legal guardian present at the appointment. The parent or guardian must be present in the studio — not just available by phone — and must consent in person. We do not have a minimum age, but use our discretion on a case-by-case basis.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-summary">What metals do you use?</summary>
        <div class="faq-body">
          <p>We offer three metal tiers:</p>
          <ul class="faq-list-inner">
            <li><strong>Tier 1 — Stainless Steel PVD:</strong> Physical Vapor Deposition coated stainless steel. Waterproof, durable, from $42.</li>
            <li><strong>Tier 2 — 14k Gold-Filled &amp; Argentium Silver:</strong> Legally regulated gold-filled (minimum 5% gold by weight) and Argentium 935 silver. From $72.</li>
            <li><strong>Tier 3 — 14k Solid Gold:</strong> 58.5% pure gold in yellow or white. Has real melt value. From $145.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>Read the full <a href="/learn/tier-guide" class="faq-link">Tier Guide</a> for a detailed breakdown.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-summary">Can I add charms later?</summary>
        <div class="faq-body">
          <p>Yes. Charm swaps are available at any time for $10 plus the cost of the new charm. We remove the existing charm and weld the new one in its place. If you want to add a charm to a chain that doesn't currently have one, the same process applies. You can have up to 3 charms on a single chain.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-summary">Do you travel for events?</summary>
        <div class="faq-body">
          <p>Yes. We offer mobile pop-ups for bridal parties, corporate events, brand activations, and private gatherings. Minimum 4 guests. Travel fee is $35 plus $2 per mile from our Santa Cruz studio. For events, pricing is per guest using our standard service rates, with a 10% group discount applied. Contact us to discuss your event.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

    </div>

    <div class="faq-footer">
      <p class="faq-footer__text">Have a question we didn't answer?</p>
      <a href="/book" class="btn btn--gold">Book a Consultation</a>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

<!-- ── Related ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<section class="section--butter section--sm">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="related-articles">
      <span class="eyebrow eyebrow--dark">Continue Reading</span>
      <div class="related-links">
        <a href="/learn/what-is-permanent-jewelry" class="related-link">What Is Permanent Jewelry?</a>
        <a href="/learn/aftercare" class="related-link">Aftercare Guide</a>
        <a href="/learn/tier-guide" class="related-link">The Tier Guide</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

</Layout>

<style is:global>
/* ── FAQ List ───────────────────────────────────────────────── */
.faq-list {
  border-top: 1px solid var(--cream-dark);
  margin-bottom: 64px;
}

.faq-item {
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--cream-dark);
}

.faq-summary {
  font-family: var(--font-body);
  font-size: 1rem;
  font-weight: 400;
  letter-spacing: 0.01em;
  color: var(--black);
  padding: 20px 0;
  cursor: pointer;
  list-style: none;
  display: flex;
  justify-content: space-between;
  align-items: center;
  user-select: none;
  transition: color 0.2s;
}

.faq-summary::-webkit-details-marker {
  display: none;
}

.faq-summary::after {
  content: '+';
  font-family: var(--font-body);
  font-size: 1.4rem;
  font-weight: 300;
  color: var(--butter-dark);
  flex-shrink: 0;
  margin-left: 24px;
  transition: transform 0.25s var(--ease);
  line-height: 1;
}

details[open] .faq-summary::after {
  transform: rotate(45deg);
}

.faq-item:hover .faq-summary {
  color: var(--butter-dark);
}

.faq-body {
  padding-bottom: 28px;
}

.faq-body p {
  font-family: var(--font-body);
  font-size: 14px;
  font-weight: 300;
  line-height: 1.85;
  color: var(--charcoal);
  opacity: 0.72;
  margin-bottom: 12px;
}

.faq-body p:last-child {
  margin-bottom: 0;
}

.faq-list-inner {
  list-style: none;
  margin: 12px 0;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 8px;
}

.faq-list-inner li {
  font-family: var(--font-body);
  font-size: 14px;
  font-weight: 300;
  line-height: 1.7;
  color: var(--charcoal);
  opacity: 0.72;
  padding-left: 16px;
  position: relative;
}

.faq-list-inner li::before {
  content: '';
  position: absolute;
  left: 0;
  top: 11px;
  width: 5px;
  height: 1px;
  background: var(--butter-dark);
}

.faq-link {
  color: var(--butter-dark);
  text-decoration: underline;
  text-underline-offset: 3px;
  font-weight: 400;
}

/* ── FAQ Footer ─────────────────────────────────────────────── */
.faq-footer {
  text-align: center;
  padding: 48px;
  border: 1px solid var(--cream-dark);
  background: var(--warm-white);
}

.faq-footer__text {
  font-family: var(--font-display);
  font-size: 1.5rem;
  font-weight: 300;
  font-style: italic;
  color: var(--black);
  opacity: 0.7;
  margin-bottom: 24px;
}
</style>
